and lo, there was much rejoicing among the people, as
  silly@ugcs.caltech.edu (Brad Threatt) writes:
>I've been playing nethack for a few days now, and I've even gotten to level
>6, but I need some advice.  My friend said that the point of the game was
>to find the Omelet of Yendor.  He said he didn't know how to get it, and 
>that was part of the fun of the game.  Well, the other day, I found an egg,
>and I'm wondering if I can make the Omelet with it.  Or do you need a special
>egg or more than one?  Also, do I need stuff to cook with to?  Thanks for
>the help.  I think I'll post some helpful hints for all of you guys.  It looks
>like you need them.

well, you're part-way there.

take the egg, hold it very carefully (don't throw it or wield it or anything
stupid like that), and carry it down through the dungeon, about 40 or so
levels.  there, you will meet the chef of yendor.  you have to kill him,
tkae his hat (the chef's hat of yendor), and find the holy stove.
while wearing the chef's hat of yendor, #offer the egg as a sacrifice to
the holy stove.  if it responds that ''you ahve a feeling of inadequacy''
then you need to find mozerrella cheese, green peppers, mushrooms,
and onions.  check the corpse of the chef or the entire kitchen room.
#offer all of these things until the stove glows.  (i don't know the
color - i haven't made it all the way down yet.)

when the stove glows, you can pick up the omelet of yendor. run (don't
walk) back up the 40-or-so levels, bring the omelet of yendor to the
endroom and find the table of the gods.  you must serve the omelet
to /your/ god (you have to know which is yours) and voila!
(french for ''you won the game'') you won the game.

easy, right?  have fun.

